# Instructions-only chat — no RE, PR, LF, login

Some workspace chats are **rules/configuration only** (agent directives, skill updates, transfer-matrix changes, Case Tracker setup, etc.). **This is not the customer-case processing chat.**

**Live automation runs only in the email processing chat** — open a separate chat with **`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`** (login, RE + Auto-LF, PR, DONE).

## When this rule applies

Treat the current chat as **instructions-only** when **any** of these is true:

1. The user **previously stated** this chat is for rules/configuration only (e.g. "this chat is for rule configuration ONLY", "do not process RE/PR/LF here").
2. The conversation is **clearly** about rules, skills, config, or automation design — **not** an active Sprinklr case thread (no visible-case RE workflow in progress for paste/send).
3. The user is asking to **retain/update rules** or agent behaviour (like this directive).

When in doubt in a mixed thread: if the user sends **only** `RE`, `PR`, `LF`, `login`, or `DONE` without rules context → **warn and refuse** case processing (for **DONE**, point them to the email processing chat).

## Blocked commands (do not run scripts or automation)

| Command | Blocked action |
|---------|----------------|
| **RE** / **re** / **RE SHOW** / **RE FILE** | read-email script, 7-step case output, RE recovery |
| **PR** / **pr** | paste reply, write-reply script |
| **LF** / **lf** / **LF TR** | fill_case_tracker.py, log form / transfer close-out |
| **login** | Sprinklr login-only / startup automation |
| **DONE** / **Done for today** | `done_for_today.py` stop script (run in case chat) |
| **`[AUTO_PIPELINE]`** (hook followup) | **DO NOT process.** The stop hook fired in this chat instead of the email processing chat. See warning below. |
| **`[AUTO_PIPELINE_TURN_C]`** | **DO NOT process.** Obsolete. Block and warn. |

**Allowed here (not case processing):** **`revert last`** — restore file checkpoint (see `.cursor/rules/revert-last.mdc`).

Also do **not** partially run case steps (no CDP Sprinklr reads "just to check" unless explicitly for **rules/testing documentation** the user asked for in this chat).

## [AUTO_PIPELINE] in instructions chat — hard block

**Root cause:** The Cursor stop hook fires in whichever chat is active when an agent turn ends. If you are in this chat when a case extract completes, `[AUTO_PIPELINE]` lands here instead of the email processing chat.

**When `[AUTO_PIPELINE]` arrives here:**

1. **Do NOT** read `latest_extract.md`, run `--pickup`, write a 7-step RE, or call `fill_case_tracker.py`.
2. Output **exactly**:

```
⚠️ Wrong chat — [AUTO_PIPELINE] fired in the instructions chat.
The stop hook should only fire in the email processing chat.

Go to the email processing chat — agent must write the 7-step and Auto-LF there.
Sounds are operator audio cues only; they do not file Case Tracker.
```

3. **Do not** assume background Auto-LF from a sound hook — that path was removed.
4. **Do not** arm `--closeout-anwenden`, `--closeout-weiter`, or any arm command here.

**Prevention:** Keep the **email processing chat** in focus during a shift. Switch to this instructions chat only between cases or after DONE.

## Mandatory warning (use every time)

When the user triggers a blocked command in an instructions-only chat, **do not process it**. Reply with this (or equivalent) **before anything else**:

```
⚠️ Wrong chat — this thread is for rules and configuration only, not Sprinklr login or email processing (RE / PR / LF).

Open a separate chat with EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md for customer cases, then run your command there.
```

If the user also asked a rules/config question in the same message, answer that **after** the warning.

## What IS allowed here

- Updating `.cursor/rules/`, skills, AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS, TransferMatrix, config structure (not live case handling)
- Explaining how RE/PR/LF/login work
- Documenting test results from configuration work **without** treating the chat as the live processing queue
- Pointing bonus / Produktivitätsbonus questions to **`SEPTEMBER-INCENTIVE-AGENT.md`** (do not deep-run bonus planning here unless the user insists)

## Model policy (this chat)

- **Instructions dashboard:** **Composer 2.5** default (user sets picker manually). **Sonnet** for complex multi-file / architecture when behind pace on included usage.
- **Email processing chat** (other thread): **Claude 4.6 Sonnet** for live RE/PR/LF.
- **Grok banned.** **On-demand Disabled** — never recommend overages. Pace to ~full included usage by month-end: `.cursor/knowledge/pro-plus-model-spend-2026.md`, `AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS.md`, `.cursor/rules/ai-model-stay-auto.mdc`.

## Customer-case chats

The **email processing agent chat** (startup: **`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`**) runs live case work:

- **login** — Sprinklr + Case Tracker tab
- **RE** — Anwenden-gated auto-RE (or `--once`) → 7-step RE
- **RE** — extract → 7-step + Auto-LF  
- **PR** — paste reply (then Anwenden arm; LF already done at RE)

